## 🧪 Testing

### Automated scenario suite
```bash
python backend/test_scan_scenarios.py
```
This runs 33 safe, medium and high-risk scenarios through `/scan`, including Gmail, Maybank2u, LHDN, `jtp-photography.com`, `bintv.cc`, gambling sites, typosquats and fake virus alerts. It uses a temporary copy of the database, so your logs are not touched, and it never connects to a malicious site. Expected result: **33/33 scenarios passed**.

### Manual tests in Chrome (safe to visit)
* **Safe browsing:** Visit `https://www.google.com` or `https://uitm.edu.my` and click **Scan Website** $\rightarrow$ **✅ SAFE**.
* **Certificate checks:** `https://expired.badssl.com/`, `https://self-signed.badssl.com/` and `https://wrong.host.badssl.com/` are public test pages with broken certificates $\rightarrow$ **⚠️ HIGH RISK** (*Invalid certificate*).
* **Scam content on an official site:** Open a Malay scam email in Gmail $\rightarrow$ **⚡ MEDIUM RISK** with the matched Bahasa Malaysia / Manglish phrases listed.
* **Allowlist bypass:** Click **+ Allowlist** on any domain and scan again $\rightarrow$ skips the engine and returns **✅ SAFE (0%)**.